\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d2583ebc070055b7023b45a8d164ad3b73261b6c6b83a6091825e00a71ce88c2","event_uuid":"46e67465-cfab-4e3d-bb9a-db18d31c87c7","position":{"commit_sha":"4e19ba361ae24ffaefe8c5a16abd2633facc4e0c","position":"1786559060517899355-46e67465-cfab-4e3d-bb9a-db18d31c87c7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786533743895115001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"026df780-70a6-451f-b733-8910b4ccd53e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9590-34f5-21a8-41fc"},{"link_uuid":"46e67465-cfab-4e3d-bb9a-db18d31c87c7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3f7d-af1a-89b9-4111"}],"description":"# The DC store-copy fixture hard-fails on `git fetch origin tickets` and swallows git's reason\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nLive External Integration run **31587452003** (2026-08-12, head `b13173bb7d`) ended the DC\nharness at `1 failed, 59 passed, 1 xfailed, 1 error in 2471.11s`. The **error** is a fixture\nfailure, not a cell defect:\n\n    ERROR tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_outbound_unassign_round_trips\n      - subprocess.CalledProcessError: Command '['git','fetch','origin','tickets']'\n        returned non-zero exit status 128.\n\nIt aborts at setup of `dc_store_copy_repo` (`tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py`,\nlines 139-141 at origin/main `cc69cc1179`), which fetches the live `tickets` branch in the\nouter CI checkout and then `git archive FETCH_HEAD | tar -x` to seed a scrubbed store copy.\n\n**Two problems, and the second is why the first is still unexplained:**\n\n1. **The failure is undiagnosable, by construction.** The call is\n   `subprocess.run(..., capture_output=True, check=True)`: `capture_output=True` routes git's\n   stderr into a captured buffer, and `check=True` then raises `CalledProcessError` whose\n   string form carries only the exit status. Git's own message — the one line that would say\n   whether this was auth, a missing ref, a refspec miss under the CI partial clone, or a\n   network error — is discarded. From the run log, exit 128 is all there is. The `git archive`\n   (142-144) and `git ls-tree` (151-156) calls beside it have the identical shape.\n2. **The fetch is a single un-retried network call** on the critical path of a 41-minute live\n   job, so any transient blip takes the cell out as an ERROR.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the diagnostic FIRST — it is what makes the retry policy decidable.\n\n* Add a module-level `_run_git(argv, cwd, ...)` helper in `_dc_fixtures.py` that runs the\n  command with captured output and, on a non-zero exit, raises `RuntimeError` carrying the\n  joined argv (which names the remote and branch), the exit status, and git's captured\n  **stderr** verbatim. Route the fetch, archive and ls-tree calls through it.\n* Then add bounded retry to the fetch only: `_fetch_tickets(...)` retries a failing fetch a\n  fixed small number of times with a backoff sleep (injectable for test), and on final failure\n  re-raises the diagnostic error. Policy is **retry-then-fail**, not retry-then-skip, so a\n  genuine misconfiguration still reds the lane rather than silently dropping coverage.\n\nThe helpers are plain module-level functions, so the unit tier can load `_dc_fixtures.py` by\npath (`importlib.util.spec_from_file_location`, the pattern already used by\n`tests/unit/test_live_dc_isolation_controls_59b2.py`) and drive them with a stubbed\n`subprocess.run` — no harness image, no live lane, verified on every commit.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py` — new `_run_git` / `_fetch_tickets` helpers;\n  the `dc_store_copy_repo` fetch/archive/ls-tree calls routed through them.\n* `tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py` — new unit cell (repo tier).\n\n## Testing\n\nAll acceptance evidence is repo-tier and runs under plain `pytest tests/unit/...`; the live\nlane is operator-spend and is NOT a gate for this ticket (see \"Follow-up\", below).\n\n* stubbed `subprocess.run` returning exit 128 with a distinctive stderr line proves the raised\n  message carries that stderr, the remote, the branch and the status — and the negative\n  control proves it goes RED against the old `check=True` shape (a `CalledProcessError` whose\n  text does not contain the stderr).\n* stubbed `subprocess.run` failing once then succeeding proves the fetch retries and returns.\n* stubbed `subprocess.run` always failing proves the attempt count is bounded and the final\n  raise still carries git's stderr.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_dc_fixtures.py`'s git fetch failure path raises an error whose message contains git's\n      captured stderr verbatim plus the remote, the branch and the exit status — proven by a\n      unit cell with a stubbed failing `subprocess.run`\n- [ ] the same holds for the `git archive` and `git ls-tree` calls in `dc_store_copy_repo`\n      (no `capture_output=True` + `check=True` pair is left in that fixture)\n- [ ] the fetch retries a transient failure a bounded number of times before failing — proven\n      by one stub that fails once then succeeds and one that always fails, the latter\n      asserting the attempt count is capped and the final error still names git's stderr\n- [ ] no cell is deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed; `make lint`, `make typecheck` and\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py` pass\n\n## Follow-up (deliberately NOT an AC here)\n\nConfirming on a live run that `test_outbound_unassign_round_trips` either passes or now fails\nwith git's actual reason requires a Live External Integration run, which is operator-spend and\ncannot be triggered from this ticket. The next scheduled live run reads the improved message;\nif it still errors, the log will finally name the cause and that becomes its own ticket.\n\n## Not in scope\n\nThe other residual in the same run —\n`test_dc_mutations.py::test_outbound_create_stamps_both_provenance_markers` failing with\n`rebar create failed (exit 1): Error: git commit failed while holding lock: git timed out\nafter 30s` — is the tracker write-lock contention family and is already tracked by\n`royal-weariless-zebrafish` (`10c3-5a33-2e25-4584`). Do not fold it in here.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py","reason":"add _run_git/_fetch_tickets helpers that surface git stderr and retry the tickets fetch; route fetch/archive/ls-tree through them"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py","reason":"new repo-tier cell driving the helpers with a stubbed subprocess.run"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3f7d-af1a-89b9-4111"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c39bcc2a-ed10-4d8f-ab81-02bc29de3246","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"00c6-e96e-3f04-434d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC store-copy fixture hard-fails on git fetch origin tickets and swallows git's stderr","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cf5b6f47-85ed-4e3b-9a45-206c5041056c","026df780-70a6-451f-b733-8910b4ccd53e","170ab5a8-b6cc-453a-9fc7-467cb498cfce","701acef4-d5b8-4052-8f7b-7c285381d824","d6bceb25-ac38-42cd-8d0a-07f4d968d944","c39bcc2a-ed10-4d8f-ab81-02bc29de3246","a0abe306-cfca-4605-8aa2-d60a0f0758bd","46e67465-cfab-4e3d-bb9a-db18d31c87c7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786559060517899356,"uuid":"5dbdc714-f0e6-4e21-8510-bf234ec6dbce"}